---
description: Keep every Innernet popup brief and free of scrolling
alwaysApply: true
---

# Popups never scroll

- Every popup, modal, dialog and popover must fit its content without horizontal or vertical scrolling, including on phones and at increased text size.
- Use popups only for brief information or a small, focused confirmation.
- If content needs scrolling, give it a normal page with ordinary document scrolling. Do not hide, clip or shrink content to keep it in a popup.
- Settings, long forms, lists and detailed reference information belong on pages. For example, source choices and storage locations live at `/sources`.
- Check both narrow and wide screens when adding or changing an overlay.
